description:
Build and read the double-null filter strings of `GetOpenFileNameW` (lesson 3.02), and work out the name a Save dialog produces:

```cpp
struct FileType { std::string description; std::string patterns; };   // patterns like "*.txt;*.md"

std::string buildFilter(const std::vector<FileType>& types);
std::vector<FileType> parseFilter(const std::string& filter);
std::string defaultExtension(const FileType& type);
std::string finalSaveName(const std::string& typed, const FileType& selected);
```

- `buildFilter`: each type gives its description, a null character, its patterns, a null; the whole string ends with one **extra** null. No types gives just `"\0"` (one null). The returned `std::string` contains the nulls.
- `parseFilter` reads such a string back; it stops at the empty description that marks the end, or at the end of the string, and ignores a description without patterns.
- `defaultExtension` is the extension of the **first** pattern, without `*.`, when it is a plain `*.ext` (letters and digits only); `*.*` or anything else gives `""`.
- `finalSaveName`: if the typed name (the part after the last `\`) contains a dot that is not its first character, the name is used as typed; otherwise the selected type's default extension is added (if there is one). Spaces at the ends of the typed name are removed first.

